# ---- About tab: spawn condition cheat sheet (0.25.0) ----
ironfarm.about.conditions.title=Iron golem spawn conditions
ironfarm.about.conditions.1=[Two paths]
Panic: a villager sees a mob hostile to villagers; group threshold 3; tries every 5 seconds.
Gossip: villagers talk to each other; group threshold 5; triggered by conversation.
ironfarm.about.conditions.2=[Individual conditions, required for every participant]
- Adult villager (babies have no sleep memory, so they fail automatically)
- Actually lay down in a bed within the last 20 minutes (24000 ticks)
- Has not seen an iron golem in the last 30 seconds
ironfarm.about.conditions.3=[Sleep window]
20 minutes is a full day cycle, and it keeps rolling.
A villager locked in a boat or minecart can never sleep, so this always fails.
Farms that keep villagers caged away from beds go dead after 20 minutes.
ironfarm.about.conditions.4=[Golem memory]
The memory lasts 599 ticks (not the 600 you often see quoted).
Detection range: a 33x33x33 cube centred on the villager, 16 blocks each way.
Scan rate: once every 10 seconds; only recorded if a golem is inside at that moment.
If a golem stays within 16 blocks for over 30 seconds, that villager stops spawning.
ironfarm.about.conditions.5=[Group counting]
Centred on the initiator, inflated by 10 blocks, at most 5 villagers counted.
Of those 5 slots, the panic path needs 3 qualified; the gossip path needs all 5.
ironfarm.about.conditions.6=[Important: participants do not need to panic]
Only the villager that starts the attempt must see the mob.
Every other villager just needs to have slept and not seen a golem.
So a farm only needs 3 villagers that can see the mob.
ironfarm.about.conditions.7=[Panic radii]
8 blocks: zombie, husk, drowned, zombie villager, vex
10 blocks: vindicator, zoglin
12 blocks: evoker, illusioner, ravager
15 blocks: pillager (largest coverage)
ironfarm.about.conditions.8=[What blocks it]
Line of sight must be clear: glass and slabs are fine, full blocks are not.
The wither and frostbite do NOT scare villagers, despite what many guides say.
A pillager must have its crossbow removed first, or it kills villagers and golems.
ironfarm.about.conditions.9=[Spawn point]
Search volume: 17x13x17 around the villager (8 blocks horizontally, 6 vertically).
Up to 10 random positions per attempt; if all are invalid the attempt is wasted.
Needs a standable floor, 2 blocks of headroom, and must not be liquid.
ironfarm.about.conditions.10=[What is NOT a condition]
"Nearby villagers have not summoned a golem in 30 seconds" does not exist; it is a common misreading.
Vanilla only tracks two memories: last slept, and recently seen a golem.
Since 1.16 villagers no longer need a profession, and village bed count is irrelevant.
ironfarm.about.conditions.src=Full details in "Iron-Golem-Spawn-Conditions.txt" in the project root, sourced from decompiled 1.21.1 bytecode.
